@startuml Weather_Forecasts_System_Design

title Weather Forecasts System - System Design (Service Architecture)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

actor "End User" as User

node "Frontend Service\n<<Web / Mobile Client>>" as Frontend

node "Authentication Service\n<<Firebase Authentication>>" as Auth

node "User Actions Server" as UserServer {
  component "Login/Sign Up, Profile,\nCity/Service Selection, Search,\nRate, Analytics & Aggregation API" as UserServerAPI
}

node "Scheduler Server" as Scheduler {
  component "Polling &\nNotification Dispatch" as SchedulerJob
}

database "Database Service" as DB

cloud "Partner Forecasting\nServices" as PartnerAPIs

cloud "Notification Providers\n(Email / SMS / Push)" as NotifyProviders

' --- Relationships ---
User --> Frontend : HTTPS

Frontend --> Auth : Firebase Client SDK:\nsign-in/sign-up/password-reset\n(UC1); account changes (UC13)
Frontend --> UserServer : REST/HTTPS\n(Bearer Firebase ID token)

UserServer --> Auth : verify ID token\n(Firebase Admin SDK);\nfetch single user's email\n(UC9 large-file download link)
UserServer --> DB : upsert user_id\n(JIT, on conflict do nothing);\nread/write cities, services,\nratings, analytics

Scheduler --> DB : read subscriptions,\nwrite forecasts
Scheduler --> Auth : batch-fetch emails\n(Firebase Admin SDK getUsers(),\nup to 100 ids per call)
Scheduler --> PartnerAPIs : poll forecasts
Scheduler --> NotifyProviders : dispatch warnings

' --- Notes ---
note right of Frontend
  Implements UC13 (Change
  Authentication Details) entirely
  client-side: calls the Firebase
  Client SDK directly for sign-in,
  sign-up, password reset, and
  account changes. No backend
  service is involved in any of
  these, and nothing is cached
  locally as a result.
end note

note right of Auth
  Sole source of truth for
  accounts: registration,
  credentials, sessions,
  username and email - none of
  it is ever copied into the app
  DB. Issues Firebase ID tokens,
  keyed by user_id (Firebase uid).
  Exposes a batch user-lookup
  call (up to 100 ids/request)
  used by UC11's notification
  dispatch.
end note

note right of DB
  Single shared datastore
  (see ER diagram) holding
  domain data: Users(user_id,
  created_at - JIT-provisioned,
  no account fields), Cities,
  Services, Forecasts, Ratings,
  Notifications, AnalyticsReports.
  No account data is stored here.
end note

note bottom of UserServer
  Implements UC1-UC10 and UC12:
  Login/Sign Up (incl. first-login JIT
  provisioning + redirect to
  City/Service selection if the
  user has no CitySite yet),
  Edit Selections (city/service
  picks only), Select
  Cities/Services, Search
  Forecast, Rate Forecasting
  Service, Request/Download
  Analytics (fetches email from
  Auth only for the large-file
  case), View Aggregated
  Forecast, Calculate Aggregates
  (invoked by UC8/UC10, both
  End User actions).
end note

note bottom of Scheduler
  Implements UC11 (Poll Forecasts
  and Notify Users). Runs
  independently of user requests
  on a fixed schedule. Batch-fetches
  recipient emails from Auth once
  per cycle rather than caching
  them locally; retries a failed
  batch with backoff before
  excluding those users for
  this cycle (see UC11 A8).
end note

@enduml
